## *Exercises*:

Strings: 
   [+] *1. Repeat Runner*
   * *Goal*: Repeat a given string a specific number of times.
   * *Input*: `"Run"`, `3`
   * *Expected Output*: `"RunRunRun"`

   [+] *2. Email Masker*
   * *Goal*: Replace the characters of an email prefix with asterisks, keeping only the first and last letter of the prefix visible before the @ symbol.
   * *Input*: "codelearn@email.com"
   * *Expected Output*: "c*******n@email.com"

   [+] *3. URL Slug Creator*
   * *Goal*: Convert a title string into a URL-friendly slug by making it lowercase and replacing spaces with hyphens.
   * *Input*: "Top 10 JavaScript Tips"
   * *Expected Output*: "top-10-javascript-tips"

   [+] *4. File Extension Extractor*
   * *Goal*: Extract and return the file extension from a full filename string.
   * *Input*: "main.app.component.ts"
   * *Expected Output*: "ts"

   [+] *5. Word Truncator*
   * *Goal*: Shorten a string to a specific length and append "..." to the end if it exceeds that length.
   * *Input*: "JavaScript is awesome", 10
   * *Expected Output*: "JavaScript..."

   [+] *6. Name Formatter*
   * *Goal*: Take a full name and return it formatted as "Lastname, Firstname".
   * *Input*: "Alan Turing"
   * *Expected Output*: "Turing, Alan"

   [+] *7. Character Counter*
   * *Goal*: Count how many times a specific letter appears inside a string (case-insensitive).
   * *Input*: `"Banana"`, `"a"`
   * *Expected Output*: `3`

   [+] *8. Word Replacer*
   * *Goal*: Find a specific word in a sentence and replace all occurrences of it with a new word.
   * *Input*: `"The cat sat on the mat"`, `"mat"`, `"couch"`
   * *Expected Output*: `"The cat sat on the couch"`

   [+] *9. Money Formatter*
   * *Goal*: Ensure a number string starts with a currency symbol (default to dollar sign `$`) and always has exactly two decimal places.
   * *Input*: `"45.5"`
   * *Expected Output*: `"$45.50"`

   [+] *10. Space Cleaner*
   * *Goal*: Remove all leading, trailing, and extra duplicate spaces from inside a sentence.
   * *Input*: `" Too many spaces "`
   * *Expected Output*: `"Too many spaces"`

Arrays:
   [+] *1. Array Multiplier*
   * *Goal*: Multiply every number inside an array by a specific factor.
   * *Input*: `[1, 2, 3, 4]`, `3`
   * *Expected Output*: `[3, 6, 9, 12]`

   [+] *2. VIP Filter*
   * *Goal*: Filter an array of user objects to return only the users who have a premium membership status.
   * *Input*: `[{name: "Alice", premium: true}, {name: "Bob", premium: false}]` // declare variable input, do the same for every example having obj manipulation
   * *Expected Output*: `[{name: "Alice", premium: true}]`

   [+] *2bis. Is Divisible by n*
   * *Goal*: Filter array of numbers divisible by n.
   * *Input*: `[1,8,123,4151, 443, 53535, 900]`, `3`
   * *Expected Output*: `[123, 53535, 900]`

   [+] *3. Total Price Calculator*
   * *Goal*: Sum up the total prices of all items listed in a shopping cart array.
   * *Input*: `[{item: "Book", price: 15}, {item: "Pen", price: 5}]`
   * *Expected Output*: `20`

   [+] *4. Specific Finder*
   * *Goal*: Search an array of products and return the first product object that matches a specific ID.
   * *Input*: `[{id: 101, name: "Shirt"}, {id: 202, name: "Shoes"}]`, `202`
   * *Expected Output*: `{id: 202, name: "Shoes"}`

   [+] *5. Inventory Checker*
   * *Goal*: Check if every single item object in an inventory array is currently in stock.
   * *Input*: `[{name: "Laptop", inStock: true}, {name: "Mouse", inStock: false}]`
   * *Expected Output*: `false`

   [+] *6. Nested Array flattener*
   * *Goal*: Take an array containing nested sub-arrays and flatten it down into a single, one-dimensional array.
   * *Input*: `[1, [2, 3], [4, [5]]]`
   * *Expected Output*: `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`

   [+] *7. Roster Organizer*
   * *Goal*: Sort an array of employee names alphabetically from A to Z.
   * *Input*: `["Zack", "Alex", "Mia", "Chris"]`
   * *Expected Output*: `["Alex", "Chris", "Mia", "Zack"]`

   [+] *8. Array Mirror*
   * *Goal*: Reverse the order of elements inside an array without changing or mutating the original source array.
   * *Input*: `["a", "b", "c"]`
   * *Expected Output*: `["c", "b", "a"]`

   [+] *9. Index Matcher*
   * *Goal*: Find and return the exact index position of a specific target element inside an array. Return -1 if it is missing.
   * *Input*: `["apple", "banana", "cherry"]`, `"banana"`
   * *Expected Output*: `1`

   [+] *10. Array Slicer*
   * *Goal*: Extract a smaller chunk from a larger array based on a start index and a specific count length.
   * *Input*: `["gold", "silver", "bronze", "platinum"]`, `1`, `2`
   * *Expected Output*: `["silver", "bronze"]`

Math:
   [+] *1. Dice Roller*
   Create a function named `rollDice()` that returns a random whole number between `1` and `6` inclusive every time it is called.

   [+] *2. Hypotenuse Calculator*
   Write a function named `getHypotenuse(a, b)` that takes the lengths of two perpendicular sides of a right-angled triangle and returns the length of the hypotenuse side.

   [+] *3. Absolute Difference*
   Create a function named `getAbsoluteDifference(num1, num2)` that calculates the difference between two numbers and always returns a positive number, regardless of which input is larger.

   [+] *4. Price Rounding Up*
   Write a function named `roundPriceUp(price)` that takes a decimal currency value (like `15.23`) and rounds it up to the next nearest whole integer.

   [+] *5. Array Range Finder*
   Create a function named `findExtremes(arr)` that accepts an array of numbers and returns an object containing the single highest number and the single lowest number from that array.

   [+] *6. Circle Area*
   Write a function named `calculateCircleArea(radius)` that computes the area of a circle based on its radius using the official mathematical constant for Pi. [1 (https://medium.com/@francesco-saviano/master-javascript-functions-5-simple-real-world-exercises-971f7b50751a), 2 (https://javascript.plainenglish.io/beginners-guide-to-object-oriented-programming-a94601ea2fbd), 3 (https://tamilcrea.medium.com/math-built-in-function-javascript-db4759e95429)]

   [+] *7. Explicit Truncation*
   Create a function named `removeDecimals(num)` that strips away all decimal points from a positive or negative number, leaving only the whole integer portion without rounding up or down.

   [+] *8. Custom Range Generator*
   Write a function named `getRandomInRange(min, max)` that accepts two integers and returns a random whole integer that falls strictly between those two limits, inclusive of both `min` and `max`.

   [+] *9. Power Trip*
   Create a function named `raiseToPower(base, exponent)` that calculates and returns the result of the base number multiplied by itself the number of times specified by the exponent. [1 (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Scripting/Math)]

   [+] *10. Digital Clock Minutes*
   Write a function named `getWholeMinutes(seconds)` that takes a large number of seconds and calculates exactly how many full, completed minutes are contained within them, discarding any remaining leftover seconds.

Objects:
   [-] 1. The Car Status
   * *Goal*: Create a function that takes a car object and updates its mileage. It should also add a new boolean property `needsService` which is `true` if the new mileage is over 100,000, and `false` otherwise.
   * *Input:* `updateCar({ brand: "Honda", mileage: 95000 }, 6000)`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ brand: "Honda", mileage: 101000, needsService: true }`

   [-] 2. The Inventory Total
   * *Goal*: Create a function that calculates the total value of an inventory object. The object keys are item names, and the values are objects containing `price` and `quantity`.
   * *Input:* ```javascript const inventory = { laptop: { price: 1000, quantity: 2 }, mouse: { price: 25, quantity: 5 } };
   * *Expected Output:* `2125`

   [-] 3. Property Filter
   * *Goal*: Create a function that takes an object and an array of keys. It should return a new object containing _only_ the properties specified in the array.
   * *Input:* `filterProps({ a: 1, b: 2, c: 3 }, ["a", "c"])`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ a: 1, c: 3 }`

   [-] 4. Frequency Counter
   * *Goal*: Create a function that takes an array of strings and returns an object representing the frequency of each string.
   * *Input:* `countWords(["apple", "banana", "apple", "cherry", "banana", "apple"])`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ apple: 3, banana: 2, cherry: 1 }`

   [-] 5. Object Inverter
   * *Goal*: Create a function that swaps the keys and values of an object. Assume all values are unique strings or numbers.
   * *Input:* `invertObject({ name: "Alice", role: "Admin" })`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ Alice: "name", Admin: "role" }`

   [-] 6. Deep Merge Basics
   * *Goal*: Create a function that combines two objects. If a key exists in both objects, the value from the second object should overwrite the first. If a key only exists in one, it should be included as-is.
   * *Input:* `mergeObjects({ a: 1, b: 2 }, { b: 9, c: 3 })`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ a: 1, b: 9, c: 3 }`

   [-] 7. Grade Averager
   * *Goal*: Create a function that takes a student object with an array of scores, calculates their average score, and adds an `average` property to the object.
   * *Input:* `addAverage({ name: "John", scores: [80, 90, 100] })`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ name: "John", scores: [80, 90, 100], average: 90 }`

   [-] 8.  Object to Query String
   * *Goal*: Create a function that converts a flat object of key-value pairs into a URL query string.
   * *Input:* `toQueryString({ search: "javascript", page: 2, filter: "recent" })`
   * *Expected Output:* `"search=javascript&page=2&filter=recent"`

   [-] 9.  Finding the MVP
   * *Goal*: Create a function that takes an object representing a team's players and their points scored, and returns the name of the player with the highest score.
   * *Input:* ```javascript const team = { Alice: 14, Bob: 22, Charlie: 18 };
   * *Expected Output:* `"Bob"`

   [-] 10. The Object Cleaner
   * *Goal*:Create a function that removes any properties from an object that have a value of `null` or `undefined`.
   * *Input:* `cleanObject({ name: "Alex", age: null, email: undefined, active: true })`
   * *Expected Output:* `{ name: "Alex", active: true }`

